#pragma once

/**
 * The machinery that drives a strategy without a broker.
 *
 * Where `<algotradelib/strategy>` is what a strategy author includes, this is what a program
 * includes to run one. It holds the context a strategy reads from, the dispatcher that calls only
 * the handlers a strategy defines, and `DryRunner`, which exercises a strategy end to end and
 * sends nothing.
 *
 * **Reaches no broker and no transport header.** A dry run holds no session, so a dry-run
 * translation unit compiles no call into TLS or HTTP and instantiates no adapter code: verified both
 * by `tests/test-runner-isolation.cpp`, which asserts it from a unit including nothing else, and by
 * symbol inspection of an installed consumer, which finds no `algotradelib::network`,
 * `algotradelib::kis` or `algotradelib::tossinvest` symbol at all.
 *
 * What it does **not** promise is that the OpenSSL library is absent from the link line. The
 * package exports one interface target that carries the transport dependencies for every consumer,
 * so a dry-run binary still has libssl as a dylib dependency it never calls. Making that literal
 * needs a second, transport-free target; see `plan/todo/offline-only-target.md`.
 *
 * `LiveRunner` is in `<algotradelib/live>` precisely because it does need them, and separating the
 * two is what keeps the compile-time half of that checkable.
 *
 * It does reach `<algotradelib/analytics>` when the library was built with a linear-algebra
 * backend, because a cached bar series is an analytics type. Without one the context simply offers
 * no series accessors, and a strategy trading on prices and positions alone is unaffected.
 */

#include "src/runner/context.hpp"
#include "src/runner/dispatch.hpp"
#include "src/runner/runner.hpp"
#include "src/runner/execution.hpp"

#include <algotradelib/strategy>
